        "original_id": "ed7ffd2b-eb96-522a-9f97-7531c7ecec51",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alison Moyet, Mike Muir, Michael Seiff\n- Bands: Suicidal Tendencies, Los Cycos, Infectious Grooves\n- Songs and Albums: When I Was Your Girl, The Minutes, Welcome to Venice\n- Organizations: Suicidal Records\n- Places: England, Venice, California\n\nFacts:\n- Alison Moyet was born on 18 June 1961 and is an English singer, songwriter, and performer noted for her bluesy contralto voice.\n- Mike Muir was born on March 14, 1963 and is the lead vocalist of the Venice, California crossover thrash bands Suicidal Tendencies and Los Cycos, and of the funk metal band Infectious Grooves.\n- \"When I Was Your Girl\" is a song by English singer-songwriter Alison Moyet.\n- \"When I Was Your Girl\" was released as the first single from Alison Moyet's eighth studio album, \"The Minutes\".\n- \"The Minutes\" debuted at number five in the UK Albums Chart on 12 May 2013.\n- \"Welcome to Venice\" was produced by Mike Muir.\n- \"Welcome to Venice\" features cover art by Michael Seiff, who later created art for the other three original Suicidal Records releases.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
